WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:04.200
This is an interesting story that I thought
I'd bring up with you today.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:10.220
There's been a debate recently over the claim
that Elizabeth Warren predicted the 2008 financial

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:15.290
crisis before it happened and most of the
focus on the story has been on the wrong thing.

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:20.020
Most of the focus has been on determining
did Elizabeth Warren predict the financial

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:23.410
crisis or did she not actually predict the
financial crisis?

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:28.640
But I don't actually think that that's the
right argument at all to be having.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:30.481
I'll tell you the facts first and then I'll
tell you why.

00:00:30.481 --> 00:00:33.949
I think the entire conversation is being framed
incorrectly.

00:00:33.949 --> 00:00:39.489
2020 Democratic candidate Elizabeth Warren
did a CNN town hall and one of the things

00:00:39.489 --> 00:00:44.390
that she said was that she predicted the 2008
financial crisis.

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:47.960
She said, quote and starting in the early
two thousands the crisis was coming.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:51.379
I was waving my arms, ringing the bell, doing
everything I could.

00:00:51.379 --> 00:00:54.149
I said, families are getting cheated all over
this country.

00:00:54.149 --> 00:00:58.239
It started when the mortgage companies targeted
communities of color.

00:00:58.239 --> 00:01:01.379
They targeted seniors, they targeted Latinos.

00:01:01.379 --> 00:01:07.000
They came in and sold the worst possible mortgages
and stripped wealth out of those communities

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.250
and then took those products across the nation.

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:11.010
I went everywhere I could.

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:14.130
I talked to about it to anyone who would listen.

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:16.420
A crisis is coming.

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:18.630
So is this true that she did this?

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:19.829
Basically it is.

00:01:19.829 --> 00:01:20.829
Okay.

00:01:20.829 --> 00:01:25.840
Before 2008 Elizabeth Warren was talking about
the impending housing and financial crisis

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:27.359
in her 2003 book.

00:01:27.359 --> 00:01:32.310
She talked about it, subprime lending and
housing crisis in 2004 on PBS.

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:36.899
She said that the growing household debt,
the growing number of risky mortgage lending

00:01:36.899 --> 00:01:40.350
practices are causing a problem.

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:44.829
In 2005 she told the New York Times that the
amount of home equity debt that homeowners

00:01:44.829 --> 00:01:47.530
were getting into was a big red flag.

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:53.249
And politifact looked at this and determined,
yes, Elizabeth Warren did predict the financial

00:01:53.249 --> 00:01:54.289
crisis.

00:01:54.289 --> 00:01:55.850
But here's my reaction.

00:01:55.850 --> 00:02:02.049
So what Elizabeth Warren did predict the financial
crisis, but why is that a big deal?

00:02:02.049 --> 00:02:03.560
Tons of people predicted it.

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:08.680
Tons are predicting another crisis now and
none of it is even remotely notable, requires

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:10.250
special insight to predict.

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:16.310
W what I mean by that is obviously our economic
system and circumstances are not sustainable.

00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:22.030
Of course, there's always a financial crisis
or a major downturn somewhere on the horizon.

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:26.550
The question is, is it a year away or four
years away or eight years away?

00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:32.150
I don't know how notable it is that Elizabeth
Warren predicted something that anyone who

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:37.770
understands the boom and bust cycles of our
economic system has been predicting.

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:42.600
As a matter of fact, for decades, uh, or for
as long as they have been following the economy,

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:48.530
these boom bust cycles are implicit and inherent
to the economic system that we have.

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:49.990
They're always on the horizon.

00:02:49.990 --> 00:02:54.920
The question is just when, so one of the reactions
to this entire Elizabeth Warren thing has

00:02:54.920 --> 00:03:00.210
been, well, we would care about whether she
did or didn't predict it because we should

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:05.220
want a president who has the foresight to
predict when the next crisis will be.

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:06.220
Well, okay.

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:11.760
That may be, but anybody who understands how
the economy works should understand that there's

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:14.150
always a looming crisis on the horizon.

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:18.650
There's always a looming downturn on the horizon
because it's implicit to the system.

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:24.690
We have the vulture capitalists cycles of
boom and bust that increase inequality and

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:32.400
increased despair don't happen less frequently
unless we actually deal with the problems

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:34.300
inherent to the system that we have.

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:39.240
So Elizabeth Warren predicted it, tons of
people predicted it, and anybody who understands

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:43.500
our system understands that such a crisis
is always on the horizon.

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:47.420
It's great that Elizabeth Warren is actually
talking about it, but having the foresight

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:50.761
to predict it is actually not notable, although
I'm glad that it is getting more attention.

